# RFC6851. MOVE copies and then removes, and reports COPYUID in an
# untagged OK before either, as RFC9051 6.4.8 requires, so that the
# client hears about the copies before it hears that the originals are
# gone.
#
# A MOVE by message number may not report the EXPUNGE while it runs:
# the client is addressing messages by number, and renumbering them
# under it is what RFC2180 4.4.1/2 warns about, so the EXPUNGE waits
# for the next command. UID MOVE has no such problem and reports it at
# once.
#
# Moving to the selected mailbox is allowed (RFC6851 3.3), and means
# the messages get new uids, since RFC9051 6.4.8 says each message
# must end up moved or unaffected, never in both places at once.
depends 20
send 1
a create "Other"
receive 1
a OK done
send 1
b select inbox
receive 8
* 20 EXISTS
* 20 RECENT
* OK [UIDNEXT 21] next uid
* FLAGS (\Answered \Deleted \Draft \Flagged \Seen)
* OK [PERMANENTFLAGS (\Answered \Deleted \Draft \Flagged \Seen \*)] permanent flags
* OK [UIDVALIDITY 1] uid validity
* OK [MAILBOXID (f...)] stable mailbox ID
b OK [READ-WRITE] done
send 1
c move 3 Other
receive 2
* OK [COPYUID 1 3 1] moved
c OK done
send 1
d noop
receive 2
* 3 EXPUNGE
d OK done
send 1
e uid move 4 inbox
receive 5
* OK [COPYUID 1 4 21] moved
* 20 EXISTS
* OK [UIDNEXT 22] next uid
* 3 EXPUNGE
e OK done
send 1
f uid fetch 19:* uid
receive 4
* 17 FETCH (UID 19)
* 18 FETCH (UID 20)
* 19 FETCH (UID 21)
f OK done
end
